-- title:
--   Local structure at a prime exactly dividing the level
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and $g$ a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. $g$ is a normalised eigenform ($a_1(g)=1$, multiplicativity of the $q$-coefficients at coprime indices, and the prime-power recursions at primes dividing and not dividing $M$) and for no proper divisor $M'$ of $M$ does there exist a normalised eigenform of level $M'$ whose $q$-coefficients agree with those of $g$ at all primes not dividing $M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals, and $\mathcal O'$ a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field and with $\lambda$ in its maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb C$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M$, $q\notin S$) such that $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$, the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$, for all such $\ell$; let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O'$. Let $\rho$ be an adic Galois representation over $\mathcal O'$: a free finite $\mathcal O'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a multiplicative map $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O'}(V)$ which is continuous for the adic filtration, and assume that for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ inducing $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X+\ell$, and that the residual representation of $\rho$ on $\operatorname{ResidueField}(\mathcal O')\otimes_{\mathcal O'}V$ is absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to an algebraic closure of the residue field). Let $q\neq\lambda$ be a prime with $q\mid M$ and $q^2\nmid M$, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ having $q$ as a nonunit. Then there are an $\mathcal O'$-submodule $L$ of $V$ and an integer $a\in\{1,-1\}$ such that $a_q(g)=a$ in $\mathbb C$; $L=\mathcal O'\cdot b_0$ for some $\mathcal O'$-basis $(b_0,b_1)$ of $V$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$; $L$ is stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$; every element of the inertia subgroup of $P$ (viewed inside $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$) acts trivially on $L$ and trivially on $V/L$, i.e. $\rho(\tau)v-v\in L$ for all $v\in V$; and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $P$ for $q$ acts on $L$ by the scalar $aq$ and on $V/L$ by the scalar $a$, i.e. $\rho(\sigma)v-av\in L$ for all $v\in V$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility at a prime exactly dividing the level for the Galois representation attached to a weight-two newform: the local representation at $q$ is special, an unramified twist of Steinberg, with the unramified quotient character taking the value $a_q(g)=\pm1$ at Frobenius, in the shape used in the level-lowering arguments of Darmon–Diamond–Taylor and Wiles. It is applied in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_forall_point_apply_eq_qCoeff_of_not_isUnramifiedAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_forall_point_apply_eq_qCoeff_of_not_isUnramifiedAt) to identify the Frobenius scalar on the inertia coinvariants with the Hecke eigenvalue $a_q(g)$.
